            "id": "s_l5_1",
            "type": "text",
            "title": "VeeValidate – The Standard",
            "content": "# VeeValidate\n\nVeeValidate is the most popular form validation library for Vue. It offers:\n- Declarative validation rules (like `required`, `email`, `min`).\n- Integration with components.\n- Schema validation with Yup.\n- Built‑in error messages.\n\n**Installation**:\n```bash\nnpm install vee-validate yup\n```\n\nExample usage:\n```vue\n<template>\n  <Form @submit=\"onSubmit\">\n    <Field name=\"email\" rules=\"required|email\" v-slot=\"{ field, errors }\">\n      <input v-bind=\"field\" type=\"email\" />\n      <span>{{ errors[0] }}</span>\n    </Field>\n    <button type=\"submit\">Submit</button>\n  </Form>\n</template>\n\n<script setup>\nimport { Form, Field } from 'vee-validate';\nconst onSubmit = (values) => console.log(values);\n</script>\n```"
        },
        {
            "id": "s_l5_2",
            "type": "text",
            "title": "Other Libraries",
            "content": "# Alternatives\n\n- **Vuelidate** – Model‑based validation, integrates with Vue's reactivity.\n- **Vue Formulate** – Provides a powerful form building syntax with built‑in validation.\n- **FormKit** – Modern form framework with validation, theming, and more.\n\nChoose based on your project needs: VeeValidate is great for complex validation, Vuelidate is lightweight, FormKit offers a full form building system."
        },
        {
            "id": "s_l5_3",
            "type": "code",
            "title": "Example: VeeValidate with Yup Schema",
            "content": "A registration form using Yup schema for validation:",
            "codeSnippet": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html>\n<head>\n  <title>VeeValidate Demo</title>\n  <script src=\"https://unpkg.com/vue@3/dist/vue.global.js\"></script>\n  <script src=\"https://unpkg.com/vee-validate@4\"></script>\n  <script src=\"https://unpkg.com/yup@1\"></script>\n</head>\n<body>\n  <div id=\"app\">\n    <vee-form @submit=\"onSubmit\">\n      <vee-field name=\"email\" as=\"input\" label=\"Email\" />\n      <vee-error-message name=\"email\" />\n      \n      <vee-field name=\"password\" as=\"input\" type=\"password\" label=\"Password\" />\n      <vee-error-message name=\"password\" />\n      \n      <button type=\"submit\">Submit</button>\n    </vee-form>\n  </div>\n\n  <script>\n    const { createApp } = Vue;\n    const { Form, Field, ErrorMessage, configure, defineRule } = VeeValidate;\n    const * as Yup = Yup;\n\n    // Define schema\n    const schema = Yup.object({\n      email: Yup.string().required().email(),\n      password: Yup.string().required().min(6)\n    });\n\n    createApp({\n      components: {\n        VeeForm: Form,\n        VeeField: Field,\n        VeeErrorMessage: ErrorMessage\n      },\n      setup() {\n        const onSubmit = (values) => {\n          alert('Submitted: ' + JSON.stringify(values));\n        };\n        return { onSubmit };\n      }\n    }).mount('#app');\n  </script>\n</body>\n</html>",
            "codeLanguage": "html",
            "canRunCode": true
        },
